  "summary": "Isolates all legacy wallet loading and migration logic into a dedicated `wallet/legacy` subdirectory and a `wallet::legacy_migration` namespace. It introduces a `LegacyWallet` subclass of `CWallet` to hold legacy-only routines, extracts `LegacyDataSPKM` into its own file, and separates legacy loading from normal descriptor wallet loading.",
  "problem": "Although Bitcoin Core no longer supports directly loading legacy wallets, legacy wallet loading and migration logic remains co-mingled with descriptor wallet code in `CWallet` and wallet database loaders. This coupling clutters the active descriptor codebase and risks accidental calls to legacy routines.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author states: \"Now that we no longer support loading legacy wallets, there is no reason to keep any of the legacy wallet loading and migration code in the main wallet objects. Having this co-mingling of never-to-be-changed legacy wallet code and new descriptor wallet code makes it difficult to implement new things into the wallet.\" (PR description)"
  ],
